  ai_summary: "A Stanford article discusses the need to redefine radiology for the next generation, touching on patient experiences like brain fog and the societal impact of mental health challenges, suggesting a broadening scope for radiologic practice."
  
  Title: Scientists turn tumor immune cells into cancer killers
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260127112137.htm
  Category: research
  Importance: 85
  ai_summary: "Researchers have developed a method to reprogram dormant immune cells within tumors to actively destroy cancer cells, representing a significant advancement in immunotherapy."
  
  Title: These nanoparticles could destroy disease proteins behind dementia and cancer
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260127112134.htm
  Category: research
  Importance: 80
  ai_summary: "Novel nanoparticles are being developed to target and eliminate disease-causing proteins in tissues, including the brain, offering a potentially less invasive approach to treating cancer and dementia."
  
  Title: The fat you can’t see could be shrinking your brain
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260127112127.htm
  Category: research
  Importance: 75
  ai_summary: "Research using advanced MRI has linked specific patterns of fat accumulation—including pancreatic fat and 'skinny fat'—to accelerated brain aging and increased risk of neurological diseases."
  
